Save into a slot the page asks for, between turns of the main loop

The page around the engine (Overseer Console) asks now and then for a save
in a given slot. The main loop takes the request at the end of a turn, when
the player could have made a quick save: outside combat and conversations,
while the game takes orders, with the player alive. The save is made the
way a quick save is once its slot is known, described as "AUTOSAVE hh:mm",
and leaves the slot the player last picked alone. Fallout 2 CE gets the
same change.

The main loop also tells the page when it starts and when it ends: while
it runs, a game is in progress.
